# Test: the accounting record of a piped line holds the typed line, its secret masked
#
# The one question: when the command part of a piped line holds a secret, does
# the TACACS+ accounting START record hold the line as typed, the secret masked
# by config.DisplayCommand and the chain intact after the masked part? The
# dispatcher's unit test (TestDispatchAccountsTypedLineWithMaskedSecret) proves
# the accountant's input; only a daemon proves the SSH route hands the
# accountant the typed line and the TACACS+ client puts it on the wire.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-pipe-chain-honored-on-every-command-surface AC-29.
# PREVENTS: a chain dropped from the accounting record (SSH splits it off
#   before dispatch today), and a secret reaching the accounting server.
#
# Red today: execMiddleware splits the chain off before dispatch, so the
#   record is `show metrics name <redacted>` with no `| count`.
#
# The secret: no operational command in the tree takes a credential keyword
# (redact.isCredentialKey) as an argument, so the line carries a bcrypt hash
# as the metric name. redact.Command masks a password hash wherever it
# stands (redact.IsPasswordHash), through config.DisplayCommand's operational
# arm, and a name that matches no sample answers an empty list, so the line
# runs and counts 0.
#
# Method: pipe-chain-unauthorized-refused.ci's daemon and `le mock tacacs`
# with no deny rule; the mock's ACCT line names the command the record
# carries, cmd and cmd-arg joined by spaces (internal/test/mock/tacacs,
# parseAcctCommand). The standalone mock writes its own stderr, so the
# command's quotes print plain (records.go Record.Line, strconv.Quote).
#
# Where the secret may stand: only in the AUTHOR request. Authorization is
# judged on the command as typed (RFC 8907 Section 6, cmd and cmd-arg,
# tacacs/authorizer.go), so masking it there would ask the server about a
# command nobody typed; the mock prints the request it received. Every
# other line holds it nowhere: no Ze log line (each starts with its date),
# no ACCT record and no AUTHEN line. The reject is per line, over the whole
# run's stderr (runner_validate.go), because a contains= reject reads every
# process's bytes in its span, the mock's AUTHOR line included.
#
# The metrics registry: `show metrics name` answers "metrics not available"
# unless a Prometheus registry is installed (handleShowMetricsQuery,
# internal/component/cmd/show/show.go), and `ze start` installs one only
# from a `telemetry prometheus` block (startStandaloneTelemetry,
# cmd/ze/hub/main_system.go), so the config carries one on $PORT3.

option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ZE_CONFIG_DIR:value=.
option=env:var=XDG_DATA_HOME:value=.
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass

stdin=init-answers:terminator=EOF_INIT
admin
testpass
127.0.0.1
$PORT2
EOF_INIT

tmpfs=aaa.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		tacacs {
			server 127.0.0.1 { port $PORT; key "ze-mock-key"; }
			timeout 2
			authorization true
			accounting true
		}
		tacacs-profile 15 { profile [ admin ]; }
	}
	authorization {
		profile admin { run { default-action allow; } edit { default-action allow; } }
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT2;
		}
	}
}
telemetry {
	prometheus {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT3;
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le mock tacacs --port $PORT --key ze-mock-key --user admin:testpass:15:name=tacacs:ready=le mock tacacs: listening on
expect=stderr:pattern=ACCT START seq=[0-9]+ total=[0-9]+ cmd="show metrics name <redacted> \| count \| json"
expect=stderr:pattern=AUTHOR cmd="show metrics name .{7}UlwuiuH82Unfsq\.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW\.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO \| count \| json"
reject=stderr:pattern=(?m)^([^t]|t[^a]|ta[^c]|tac[^a]|taca[^c]|tacac[^s]|tacacs[^-]).*UlwuiuH82Unfsq
reject=stderr:pattern=(?m)^tacacs-mock: (ACCT|AUTHEN).*UlwuiuH82Unfsq
reject=stderr:pattern=ACCT START .*cmd="show metrics name <redacted>"

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze init:stdin=init-answers:exit=0
cmd=background:seq=3:exec=ze start aaa.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.

cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze cli -c "show metrics name $2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO | count | json":exit=0
expect=stdout:pattern="count": ?0

cmd=stop:seq=5:name=daemon:signal=term
cmd=stop:seq=6:name=tacacs:signal=term
